{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Let YHWH, Elohim of the spirits of all flesh, appoint.</b> You who know the spirit of each and every one, and who is worthy to be appointed over them." "<b>Who shall go out before them.</b> In war. <b>And who shall come in before them, and who shall lead them out.</b> Not through another, and not like the kings of the nations, who send forth their troops while they sit in their houses — but rather as I did with Sihon and Og, as it says (Deuteronomy 3:2): ״אל תירא אותו״, and in the manner that Joshua did, as it says (Joshua 5:13): ״וילך יהושע אליו ויאמר לו הלנו אתה אם לצרינו״, and so it says of David (I Samuel 18:16): ״כי הוא יוצא ובא לפניהם״ — going out at the head and coming in at the head."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:33.835177717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}